// Scoped tsconfig for `api/` only — DO NOT delete or fold back into the parent
// `detail-hub/tsconfig.json`. Vercel's Node.js function builder (`@vercel/node`)
// compiles `api/[...path].ts` by resolving the *nearest* tsconfig.json to that file
// (TypeScript's `findConfigFile`, walking up from the entrypoint's directory), and it
// forces `noEmit: false` to actually emit JS for the deployed function.
//
// The parent tsconfig sets `noEmit: true` + `allowImportingTsExtensions: true` (both
// correct there — Vite bundles `src/`, `tsc` only type-checks it). But
// `allowImportingTsExtensions` requires `noEmit`/`emitDeclarationOnly` to be set, so
// once Vercel forces `noEmit: false`, that combination throws TS5096 and the build
// fails with "Emit skipped". This file exists so the function compiles under
// emit-compatible settings without touching the parent config's `src/` behavior.
// The parent tsconfig's `include` still covers `api/**/*` for `pnpm run typecheck`,
// so this file is type-checked twice (locally in noEmit mode, and by Vercel for real
// emit) — that's intentional, not redundant. Confirmed via `@vercel/node`'s actual
// installed source (`node_modules/@vercel/node/dist/index.js` in a global `vercel`
// CLI install) — this isn't a guess.
//
// IMPORTANT: every `compilerOptions` key below is set explicitly, NOT left to inherit
// from `tsconfig.base.json` via `extends`. `extends` is still present (harmless, and
// kept in case some future, not-yet-discovered option depends on it), but nothing in
// this file's actual compilation behavior should rely on it — someone should be able
// to delete the `extends` line entirely and get identical results.
//
// Why: Vercel's builder reads this file's raw, UNMERGED JSON *before* resolving
// `extends`, to decide which compiler options to force its own default for. It only
// skips forcing a default when it sees the key already present in this file's own
// `compilerOptions` — it does not care what `extends` would otherwise resolve to. This
// has bitten us three separate times now, each time for a different key that was only
// present via `extends`:
//   - `module` undefined here → forced to `NodeNext` (+ `moduleResolution: NodeNext`,
//     `strict: false`), which rejects the extension-less relative imports used
//     throughout `api-server/src/**` (that source is written/typechecked assuming
//     `moduleResolution: bundler`, matching its own tsconfig).
//   - `target` undefined here → forced to `ES2021` regardless of the base config's
//     `es2022`.
//   - `esModuleInterop` left unset → forced to `true`, which made `pino-http`'s
//     default import type as non-callable in `api-server/src/app.ts` ("This
//     expression is not callable"). Set to `false` here (not left unset) to match
//     `api-server`'s own tsconfig, which doesn't set it either (defaults to `false`).
//   - `useUnknownInCatchVariables` left unset (only present via `extends` from
//     `tsconfig.base.json`) → forced to `false`, so `err` in `catch (err) { if (err
//     instanceof APIError) ... }` blocks in `api-server/src/routes/auth.ts` stayed
//     `any` pre-narrowing instead of `unknown`, and TS18046 fired on every property
//     access even behind the `instanceof` guard. Set to `true` here explicitly to
//     match `tsconfig.base.json` (and what `api-server`'s own typecheck actually
//     uses, since `api-server/tsconfig.json` doesn't override it either).
//
// Every other key below is copied from `tsconfig.base.json` (or, where
// `api-server/tsconfig.json` overrides a base value — e.g. `types` — matched to what
// `api-server`'s own effective/resolved tsconfig actually uses, not blindly copied
// from the base) for the same reason: so there's nothing left, of any kind, that
// Vercel's raw-JSON-peek could still silently default. If a future deploy surfaces
// yet another key in this family, the fix is to add it here explicitly, matching
// `api-server`'s effective config for that key — not to guess further ahead of time.
//
// PREVIOUSLY-FIXED BLOCKER (kept here for history, not still open): an earlier deploy
// attempt failed under Vercel's builder with `Property 'use' does not exist on type
// 'Express'` from `api-server/src/app.ts`, root-caused to `@vercel/node`'s
// `ts.LanguageService` host not implementing `realpath`, so `@types/express`'s nested
// `@types/express-serve-static-core` dependency (living only inside `.pnpm/...`, not
// as an ancestor of the symlinked `node_modules/@types/express` path) never resolved.
// Fixed on the `api-server` side by promoting `@types/express-serve-static-core` to a
// direct devDependency of `api-server` (see `artifacts/api-server/package.json` and
// commit `a9bd208`) — not something this file could fix. Not this file's concern
// going forward; noted only so the symptom is recognizable if it ever regresses.
//
// KNOWN REMAINING BLOCKER (as of this writing, NOT fixable from this file — needs a
// change in `artifacts/api-server`, out of `detail-hub`'s scope): a real Vercel deploy
// still fails with `'err' is of type 'unknown'` (TS18046) at every
// `if (err instanceof APIError) { ... }` block in `api-server/src/routes/auth.ts`,
// even with every `compilerOptions` key above made fully explicit (confirmed via a
// standalone reproduction: constructing the exact same `ts.LanguageService` +
// `ts.CompilerOptions` that `@vercel/node`'s builder constructs from this file,
// `service.getSemanticDiagnostics()` on `auth.ts` reproduces all 12 diagnostics
// deterministically, at the exact reported lines, with this file's options as-is) and
// even though `pnpm run typecheck` (real `tsc`, not `@vercel/node`'s LanguageService)
// passes clean. So this is NOT a config-completeness problem — it's the *exact same*
// root cause as the `Property 'use' does not exist` blocker above, just hitting a
// different package this time: `@vercel/node`'s `ts.LanguageService` host has no
// `realpath`, so it resolves imports through pnpm's symlinks without dereferencing
// them. `better-auth/dist/api/index.d.mts` imports `APIError` from `@better-auth/core`
// (a package-boundary crossing, not a same-package relative import) — `@better-auth/core`
// lives only inside `better-auth`'s own resolved `.pnpm/.../node_modules/@better-auth/core`
// (itself another symlink, one level down from the `better-auth` symlink), and is NOT a
// direct dependency of `api-server`, so it's not hoisted to
// `api-server/node_modules/@better-auth/core`. Without `realpath`, the non-dereferenced
// symlink chain never resolves `@better-auth/core`'s types, `APIError`'s type collapses
// to an unresolvable/`any`-like type, `err instanceof APIError` stops narrowing, and
// `err` stays `unknown` at every access afterward. Confirmed directly: temporarily
// symlinking `artifacts/api-server/node_modules/@better-auth/core` to
// `@better-auth+core@1.6.26_.../node_modules/@better-auth/core` (matching what pnpm
// would create for a direct dependency) made the same reproduction script report 0
// diagnostics. The fix belongs in `artifacts/api-server/package.json`: add
// `"@better-auth/core": "1.6.26"` (matching the version already resolved in the
// lockfile) as a direct dependency, mirroring the `@types/express-serve-static-core`
// fix above — ask backend-engineer, don't add it here.
{
  "extends": "../../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "include": ["**/*"],
  "compilerOptions": {
    // --- From tsconfig.base.json, copied verbatim (api-server doesn't override these) ---
    "incremental": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "lib": ["es2022"],
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "noEmitOnError": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": false,
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noImplicitAny": true,
    "noImplicitThis": true,
    "strictNullChecks": true,
    "strictFunctionTypes": false,
    "strictBindCallApply": true,
    "strictPropertyInitialization": true,
    "useUnknownInCatchVariables": true,
    "alwaysStrict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "target": "es2022",
    "customConditions": ["workspace"],

    // --- From api-server/tsconfig.json's own override of the base value ---
    "types": ["node"],

    // --- Local to this file: emit-related and Vercel-forced-default-avoidance,
    // not present in either base or api-server (api-server doesn't need these
    // since it's compiled by its own build.mjs/esbuild, not tsc via a
    // discovered-nearest-tsconfig.json the way @vercel/node compiles this file) ---
    "noEmit": false,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "esModuleInterop": false
  }
}
